# Pocket Ledger Server — language + intro (global)

When editing `C:\Balgram\PocketLedger-Server\sub-server\pb_public` **or** Main panel language (`main-server/public`). Same language list on both (`languages.js` from sub). Main-only keys stay in Main `i18n.js` (merge, do not replace). Details: `.cursor/rules/pl-main-sub-together.mdc`.

When editing `C:\Balgram\PocketLedger-Server\sub-server\pb_public`:

- **UI language** (`t()`, `data-i18n`): every label, button, and menu — including JS-rendered App Setting (`#as-body`). Language Save must **repaint** App Setting (`PLAppSettings.relabel` → `paint()`), not only `setTitle()`.
- **Intro language** (`ti()`, `data-intro` / class `intro`): every help / info sentence, including App Setting page intro and settings hints. Fallback `ti(key) || t(key)`.
- **One ⓘ / Hide state** panel-wide (`plIntro`, `pl_server_intros`). Any ⓘ shows **all** intros; any Hide hides **all**. App Setting intros join the same scan after paint.
- Do not bake English (or UI-only `t()`) into App Setting help HTML. Labels stay `t()`; help stays `ti()`.
